      "text": "From the given information, we know that the pressure of a gas is inversely proportional to its volume. This can be represented by the equation:\n\n\\[ P \\cdot V = k \\]\n\nwhere \\( P \\) is the pressure, \\( V \\) is the volume, and \\( k \\) is a constant.\n\nGiven that the initial pressure \\( P_1 \\) is 5 kPa and the initial volume \\( V_1 \\) is 2.28 liters, we can find the constant \\( k \\) as follows:\n\n\\[ k = P_1 \\cdot V_1 = 5 \\, \\text{kPa} \\cdot 2.28 \\, \\text{L} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the new pressure \\( P_2 \\) when the volume changes to 5.7 liters. Using the same constant \\( k \\), we can set up the equation for the new pressure:\n\n\\[ P_2 \\cdot V_2 = k \\]\n\nSubstituting the known values:\n\n\\[ P_2 \\cdot 5.7 \\, \\text{L} = 5 \\, \\text{kPa} \\cdot 2.28 \\, \\text{L} \\]\n\nSolving for \\( P_2 \\):\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{5 \\, \\text{kPa} \\cdot 2.28 \\, \\text{L}}{5.7 \\, \\text{L}} \\]\n\n\\[ P_2 = \\frac{11.4 \\, \\text{kPa} \\cdot \\text{L}}{5.7 \\, \\text{L}} \\]\n\n\\[ P_2 = 2 \\, \\text{kPa} \\]\n\nTherefore, the new pressure in the 5.7 liter container is \\(\\boxed{2}\\) kPa.",
